# Xfuzz — Third-Party Notices

Xfuzz is proprietary software (see LICENSE). It incorporates third-party
components that remain subject to their own license terms.

This file is the authoritative inventory of those components. It is verified in
CI by `tools/licensecheck`: every module required by `go.mod` must appear in the
Components table below with an allowed license, and every listed license must be
in the allowed set. A dependency added without a NOTICE entry fails the build.

See docs/adr/ADR-0018-proprietary-commercial-license.md for why this is enforced
mechanically rather than audited before release.

## Policy

| Class | Licenses | Rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Allowed | Apache-2.0, MIT, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, Unlicense, Zlib, BSD-3-Clause-Clear | Permitted with attribution below |
| Conditional | MPL-2.0 | Permitted only as an unmodified library |
| Forbidden | GPL-2.0, GPL-3.0, AGPL-3.0, LGPL-2.1, LGPL-3.0, SSPL-1.0, BUSL-1.1, CC-BY-NC-4.0 | Never |

Much of the existing fuzzing ecosystem is GPL-licensed. ADR-0001's decision to
build a novel engine with no runtime dependency on those projects is also what
keeps this policy tenable: Xfuzz interoperates with them only at the level of
data formats and wire protocols, which carry no license obligation.

Reimplementing an algorithm from a GPL-licensed source is prohibited.
Reimplementation from published papers and specifications is the required path.

